                        <h1 class="mb-4">About US</h1>
                        <p>
                            Nenneh Preparatory School was founded by Ms. Remi Saunders in 2001, 
                            after the war in Sierra Leone, to help the many displaced children. 
                            As a result of the war, hundreds of homeless and orphaned children who 
                            were separated from their families or whose parents were killed were 
                            brought to Freetown. The Nenneh Children Fund, a 501c not for profit 
                            organization, created a school to help some of the 30 displaced children 
                            ages 3 to 7 years old. The school’s motto is, Learning is the Light to Life.
                        </p>
                        <p class="mt-4">
                            In recent years, the staff at Nenneh Preparatory School observed a decline in 
                            student enrollment due to the poverty which is prevalent among the average 
                            everyday citizens of Sierra Leone. To address this issue, Nenneh Children 
                            Fund has launched a Go Fund Me Scholarship Campaign to raise funds which 
                            will be used to pay the tuition for over 100 students for the upcoming 
                            school year. Your financial support of this great cause will help 
                            children in Sierra Leone obtain the basic education that every 
                            child in the world should have.
                        </p>
